     3	## What is proven
     4	
     5	Under the supplied `MPY` semantics, the exact translated body of
     6	`x_or_y(n, x, y)` has the following partial-correctness property for every
     7	`N:Int` and every modeled values `X:Val` and `Y:Val`:
     8	
     9	- if `N < 2`, the returned value is `Y`;
    10	- if `N >= 2` and some integer `I` with `2 <= I < N` divides `N`, the
    11	  returned value is `Y`;
    12	- otherwise, the returned value is `X`.
    13	
    14	For integers, this is exactly “return `x` when `n` is prime and `y`
    15	otherwise.” The reachability proof is a partial-correctness proof; termination
    16	is not a separately proved liveness result.
    17	
    18	## Formal claim
    19	
    20	The target claim `[x-or-y]` starts from the complete initial MPY configuration,
    21	loads the exact `FuncDef` constructor emitted in `solution.mpy`, resolves and
    22	calls `x_or_y`, executes its body, returns, removes the call frame, and reaches
    23	`?V:Val` with:
    24	
    25	```k
    26	ensures ?V ==K xOrYSpec(N, X, Y)
    27	```
    28	
    29	The total entry summary is:
    30	
    31	```text
    32	xOrYSpec(N, X, Y) = Y                         when N < 2
    33	xOrYSpec(N, X, Y) = trialChoice(N, 2, X, Y)  when N >= 2
    34	```
    35	
    36	On its used domain `I >= 2`, `trialChoice(N,I,R,Y)` returns `R` at
    37	`I >= N`. At `I < N`, it advances to `I + 1`, carrying `Y` if `I` divides
    38	`N`, and otherwise carrying `R`. Thus an initial `R = X` survives exactly when
    39	no candidate divisor in `2 .. N-1` divides `N`.
    40	
    41	The loop claim `[trial-loop]` supplies the circularity:
    42	
    43	- Base: when `I = N`, the guard is false and `trialChoice(N,I,R,Y)` reduces
    44	  to `R`.
    45	- Divisor step: the real `%` comparison assigns `Y`, increments `I`, and
    46	  matches the divisor recurrence.
    47	- Non-divisor step: the real comparison preserves `R`, increments `I`, and
    48	  matches the other recurrence.
    49	- Entry discharge: the function reaches the loop with `I = 2`, `R = X`, and
    50	  `N >= 2`; the early return handles `N < 2`.
    51	
